# Keep the committed knowledge graph (.graphify/graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md,
# manifest.json, scope.json) current with the code that was just committed.
# Structural rebuild only (--no-description): no LLM backend is configured in
# this repo, and node-description generation is not needed for the committed
# artefacts. Semantic re-authoring (.graphify_semantic.json) is a separate,
# judgment-based step — see .opencode/skills/graphify/SKILL.md.
npx graphifyy@latest update . --scope all --no-description

# Stage the refreshed portable artefacts so they ride along with the next
# commit. Never auto-commits — respects the repo's no-surprise-commits rule.
#
# NOTE: the staged diff will always show scope.json/GRAPH_REPORT.md's "head"
# one commit behind — that's expected (the hook runs after the commit is
# sealed, so it can only describe the commit that just happened). Do NOT
# create a standalone "refresh the graph" commit to close that gap; doing so
# just advances HEAD again and reproduces the same one-commit lag immediately.
# Let this staged delta ride along with whatever your next real commit is.
git add .graphify/graph.json .graphify/GRAPH_REPORT.md .graphify/manifest.json .graphify/scope.json 2>/dev/null || true
